window.MG_LAZY_DATA["data/lazy/owner-courses/b383-738aca68fde905b9.json"]={sha256:"738aca68fde905b9794f98b77e5a245089b208ef98947a511266abdbd9bbd918",value:{"id":"b383","title":"轉乘車站垂直動線","titleEn":"Vertical circulation in interchange stations","category":"rail","kind":"course","status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","summary":"本課聚焦轉乘樓層高差通道分流與等候整合。從樓梯出口有效淨寬建立物理或資訊邊界，接著把扶梯下端積壓與垂直運輸往返節拍連成可驗證的介面，最後以跨層動線驗證安排整理證據。學徒逐一完成機制推導、數值算例、失效辨識及參數實驗，所有練習限定在離線模型或隔離教具，保留假設與量測的不確定度。","summaryEn":"This course studies transfer-level changes route splitting and waiting integration. Start with effective width at stair exits to define physical or information boundaries, connect accumulation at escalator landings with round-trip vertical-service cycle as verifiable interfaces, and organize evidence through planning multilevel route verification. Each unit develops a mechanism, numerical example, failure diagnosis and parameter experiment in an offline model or isolated teaching rig, retaining assumptions and measurement uncertainty.","scope":"依公開工程原理、官方資料與規範架構編寫的原創教學；步驟是可驗證的學習任務與假想算例，不是設計圖說、施工計畫、軌道進入、牽引供電隔離或列車營運許可，也不是任何專案的設計文件。數值均為教學假設或公開資料，實際工程須由合格技師依規範與實測資料重新計算並簽證。","scopeEn":"Original teaching built from public engineering principles, official sources and code frameworks. Steps are verifiable learning tasks and hypothetical exercises, not design drawings, method statements, track-access, traction-power isolation or train-operation permits, or any project's design documents. Numbers are teaching assumptions or public data; real work must be recalculated and certified by qualified engineers using codes and measured data.","subcategory":"rail-integration","subcategoryTitle":"車站機廠與系統整合","subcategoryTitleEn":"Stations depots and integration","learningTrack":"rail","learningSubdiscipline":"rail-integration","learningTags":["rail","rail-integration","station"],"architectureFamily":"rail-integration","architectureNodes":[["轉乘到達","Transfer arrivals"],["樓梯路徑","Stair route"],["電梯等候","Lift waiting"],["匯流平台","Merge landing"],["路徑量測","Route measurement"]],"architectureEdges":[[0,1],[1,2],[2,3],[3,4],[4,1]],"diagram":{"type":"rail-integration","labels":["轉乘到達","樓梯路徑","電梯等候","匯流平台","路徑量測"],"labelsEn":["Transfer arrivals","Stair route","Lift waiting","Merge landing","Route measurement"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"workedExample":{"title":"原創假想算例與邊界","titleEn":"Original hypothetical example and boundaries","text":"原創整合工作單，所有輸入均為教學假設而非代表工程實測：先研究樓梯出口有效淨寬。原創假想教學輸入：有效淨寬 width=2.4 m；假想單位寬流率 specific=1.1 persons/(m*s)。公式 y=width*specific，代入得 y=2.64 persons/s。邊界：均勻單向流的教學係數，不是法定疏散容量或規範值。敏感度只改 width=2.4 至 2.64 m，輸出變為 2.904 persons/s；離散計數採整數變化。再獨立研究跨樓層轉乘時間：原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=120 m；假想步速 speed=0.8 m/s；等待時間 wait=35 s。公式 y=distance/speed+wait，代入得 y=185 s。邊界：定步速與固定等待的概念估算，未含煙氣、擁擠及協助需求分布。兩個結果不能因同一課程就任意相加，必須先確認單位、因果順序及共同邊界。本單元辨認樓梯、扶手與下游門口的最窄斷面，檢查雙向人流是否共用同一有限寬度。最後提出一項量測能區分模型假設失效與儀器偏差，將輸入表、重算結果和適用限制一併交付。","textEn":"Original integrated worksheet; every input is a teaching assumption rather than a measurement from a reference project. First investigate effective width at stair exits. Original hypothetical teaching inputs: effective clear width width=2.4 m; hypothetical specific flow specific=1.1 persons/(m*s). Formula y=width*specific gives y=2.64 persons/s. Boundary: Teaching coefficient for uniform one-way flow, not a statutory evacuation capacity or code value. For sensitivity, change only width=2.4 to 2.64 m; the output becomes 2.904 persons/s. Discrete counts use whole-number steps. Independently investigate travel time between levels: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: walking distance distance=120 m; assumed walking speed speed=0.8 m/s; waiting time wait=35 s. Formula y=distance/speed+wait gives y=185 s. Boundary: Constant speed and fixed waiting; smoke, crowd interaction and distribution of assistance needs are omitted. Results cannot be added merely because they belong to the same course: check units, causal sequence and shared boundaries first. Locate the narrowest section among stairs, handrails and downstream doors, checking whether opposing flows share the same limited width. Propose one measurement distinguishing a failed model assumption from instrument bias, and deliver the input table, recomputed results and applicability limits together.","assumptions":"數值是本課自行設定的教學假設，不代表任何專案的設計值、量測值或規範允許值；改變系統邊界或荷載組合後必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Inputs are teaching assumptions, not any project's design values, measurements or code allowances; recalculate after changing the system boundary or load combination.","sourceScope":"原創數值練習；來源支援公開原理與工程背景，不宣稱來源提供這組數據。","sourceScopeEn":"Original numerical exercise; sources support public principles and project context, not these numbers."},"depth":5,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"simulationOnly":true,"educationEdition":16,"enrichmentVersion":16,"stages":[{"id":"b383-v16-s1","title":"樓梯出口有效淨寬與跨樓層轉乘時間","titleEn":"Effective width at stair exits & Travel time between levels","description":"本階段聚焦「樓梯出口有效淨寬」與「跨樓層轉乘時間」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Effective width at stair exits\" and \"Travel time between levels\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b383-v16-01","title":"樓梯出口有效淨寬：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Effective width at stair exits: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"objective":"說明「樓梯出口有效淨寬」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Effective width at stair exits” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元辨認樓梯、扶手與下游門口的最窄斷面，檢查雙向人流是否共用同一有限寬度。通道容量與有效淨寬有關，但扶手、門扇、行李及靠邊避讓會減少可用寬度。單位寬流率是情境參數，受方向、坡度與群體能力影響；多條通道的容量只有在下游沒有共同瓶頸時才能直接相加。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻單向流的教學係數，不是法定疏散容量或規範值。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「樓梯出口有效淨寬」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Locate the narrowest section among stairs, handrails and downstream doors, checking whether opposing flows share the same limited width. Passage capacity depends on effective clear width, reduced by rails, door leaves, luggage and edge avoidance. Specific flow is scenario dependent and varies with direction, slope and user capability. Parallel passage capacities may be added only when they do not share a downstream bottleneck. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Teaching coefficient for uniform one-way flow, not a statutory evacuation capacity or code value. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Effective width at stair exits” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：有效淨寬 width=2.4 m；假想單位寬流率 specific=1.1 persons/(m*s)。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: effective clear width width=2.4 m; hypothetical specific flow specific=1.1 persons/(m*s).","failure":"常見誤解：「兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「樓梯出口有效淨寬」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Effective width at stair exits”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-01-k1","title":"樓梯出口有效淨寬","titleEn":"Effective width at stair exits","text":"本單元辨認樓梯、扶手與下游門口的最窄斷面，檢查雙向人流是否共用同一有限寬度。通道容量與有效淨寬有關，但扶手、門扇、行李及靠邊避讓會減少可用寬度。","textEn":"Locate the narrowest section among stairs, handrails and downstream doors, checking whether opposing flows share the same limited width. Passage capacity depends on effective clear width, reduced by rails, door leaves, luggage and edge avoidance.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-01-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「樓梯出口有效淨寬」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Effective width at stair exits\" is correct?","options":["兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加","本單元辨認樓梯、扶手與下游門口的最窄斷面，檢查雙向人流是否共用同一有限寬度。","平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑"],"optionsEn":["Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity.","Locate the narrowest section among stairs, handrails and downstream doors, checking whether opposing flows share the same limited width.","The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元辨認樓梯、扶手與下游門口的最窄斷面，檢查雙向人流是否共用同一有限寬度。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Locate the narrowest section among stairs, handrails and downstream doors, checking whether opposing flows share the same limited width. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":1},{"id":"b383-v16-02","title":"樓梯出口有效淨寬：定量估算","titleEn":"Effective width at stair exits: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-01"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「樓梯出口有效淨寬」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Effective width at stair exits” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：有效淨寬 width=2.4 m；假想單位寬流率 specific=1.1 persons/(m*s)。公式 y=width*specific，代入得 y=2.64 persons/s。邊界：均勻單向流的教學係數，不是法定疏散容量或規範值。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: effective clear width width=2.4 m; hypothetical specific flow specific=1.1 persons/(m*s). Formula y=width*specific gives y=2.64 persons/s. Boundary: Teaching coefficient for uniform one-way flow, not a statutory evacuation capacity or code value. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：量測最窄位置的有效淨寬，將各方向流量分開統計，檢查下游是否出現排隊。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure clear width at the narrowest section, count each travel direction separately, and inspect downstream queues.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-02-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：有效淨寬 width=2.4 m；假想單位寬流率 specific=1.1 persons/(m*s)。公式 y=width*specific，代入得 y=2.64 persons/s。邊界：均勻單向流的教學係數，不是法定疏散容量或規範值。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: effective clear width width=2.4 m; hypothetical specific flow specific=1.1 persons/(m*s). Formula y=width*specific gives y=2.64 persons/s. Boundary: Teaching coefficient for uniform one-way flow, not a statutory evacuation capacity or code value.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-02-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「樓梯出口有效淨寬」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Effective width at stair exits\", which statement holds?","options":["出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊","整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠","原創假想教學輸入：有效淨寬 width=2.4 m；假想單位寬流率 specific=1.1 persons/(m*s)。"],"optionsEn":["Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.","A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: effective clear width width=2.4 m; hypothetical specific flow specific=1.1 persons/(m*s)."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：有效淨寬 width=2.4 m；假想單位寬流率 specific=1.1 persons/(m*s)。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: effective clear width width=2.4 m; hypothetical specific flow specific=1.1 persons/(m*s). Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":2},{"id":"b383-v16-03","title":"樓梯出口有效淨寬：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Effective width at stair exits: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-02"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「樓梯出口有效淨寬」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Effective width at stair exits” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"量測最窄位置的有效淨寬，將各方向流量分開統計，檢查下游是否出現排隊。以「樓梯出口有效淨寬」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure clear width at the narrowest section, count each travel direction separately, and inspect downstream queues. For effective width at stair exits, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把有效淨寬 width 從 2.4 改成 2.64 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 2.64 變為 2.904 persons/s。先說明「樓梯出口有效淨寬」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only effective clear width width from 2.4 to 2.64 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 2.64 to 2.904 persons/s. Explain the causal direction for effective width at stair exits, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：以建築軸線寬度代替淨寬會高估容量，出口匯流也可能讓上游兩條通道互相阻塞。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Using structural width instead of clear width overstates capacity; merging exits can make two upstream passages obstruct each other. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-03-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"量測最窄位置的有效淨寬，將各方向流量分開統計，檢查下游是否出現排隊。以「樓梯出口有效淨寬」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure clear width at the narrowest section, count each travel direction separately, and inspect downstream queues. For effective width at stair exits, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-03-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把有效淨寬 width 從 2.4 改成 2.64 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 2.64 變為 2.904 persons/s。先說明「樓梯出口有效淨寬」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only effective clear width width from 2.4 to 2.64 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 2.64 to 2.904 persons/s. Explain the causal direction for effective width at stair exits, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「樓梯出口有效淨寬」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Effective width at stair exits\"?","options":["量測最窄位置的有效淨寬，將各方向流量分開統計，檢查下游是否出現排隊。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口"],"optionsEn":["Measure clear width at the narrowest section, count each travel direction separately, and inspect downstream queues.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner."],"answer":0,"explanation":"量測最窄位置的有效淨寬，將各方向流量分開統計，檢查下游是否出現排隊。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure clear width at the narrowest section, count each travel direction separately, and inspect downstream queues. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":3},{"id":"b383-v16-04","title":"樓梯出口有效淨寬：失效診斷","titleEn":"Effective width at stair exits: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-03"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「樓梯出口有效淨寬」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Effective width at stair exits” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"以建築軸線寬度代替淨寬會高估容量，出口匯流也可能讓上游兩條通道互相阻塞。回到「樓梯出口有效淨寬」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Using structural width instead of clear width overstates capacity; merging exits can make two upstream passages obstruct each other. Trace the input chain for effective width at stair exits. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻單向流的教學係數，不是法定疏散容量或規範值。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Teaching coefficient for uniform one-way flow, not a statutory evacuation capacity or code value.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-04-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"以建築軸線寬度代替淨寬會高估容量，出口匯流也可能讓上游兩條通道互相阻塞。回到「樓梯出口有效淨寬」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Using structural width instead of clear width overstates capacity; merging exits can make two upstream passages obstruct each other. Trace the input chain for effective width at stair exits. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-04-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「樓梯出口有效淨寬」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Effective width at stair exits\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","以建築軸線寬度代替淨寬會高估容量，出口匯流也可能讓上游兩條通道互相阻塞。","平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Using structural width instead of clear width overstates capacity; merging exits can make two upstream passages obstruct each other.","The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以建築軸線寬度代替淨寬會高估容量，出口匯流也可能讓上游兩條通道互相阻塞。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Using structural width instead of clear width overstates capacity; merging exits can make two upstream passages obstruct each other. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":1,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":4},{"id":"b383-v16-05","title":"跨樓層轉乘時間：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Travel time between levels: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-04"],"objective":"說明「跨樓層轉乘時間」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Travel time between levels” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元將長距離步行與電梯等待分開記錄，對照不同轉乘路線的可達性和到達時間分布。總旅行時間應同時計入移動與等待，不能只比較平面上的最短距離。坡道、門扇與轉乘決策都可能造成停頓；對行動受限旅客而言，較遠但連續可達的路徑往往比短而不連續的路徑更可用。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定步速與固定等待的概念估算，未含煙氣、擁擠及協助需求分布。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跨樓層轉乘時間」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Record long walking segments separately from elevator waits, comparing accessibility and arrival-time distributions across transfer routes. Travel time includes movement and waiting rather than plan distance alone. Ramps, doors and transfer decisions can introduce pauses. For a mobility-limited traveller, a longer continuously accessible route can be more usable than a shorter route containing an inaccessible interruption. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant speed and fixed waiting; smoke, crowd interaction and distribution of assistance needs are omitted. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Travel time between levels” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=120 m；假想步速 speed=0.8 m/s；等待時間 wait=35 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: walking distance distance=120 m; assumed walking speed speed=0.8 m/s; waiting time wait=35 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「跨樓層轉乘時間」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Travel time between levels”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-05-k1","title":"跨樓層轉乘時間","titleEn":"Travel time between levels","text":"本單元將長距離步行與電梯等待分開記錄，對照不同轉乘路線的可達性和到達時間分布。總旅行時間應同時計入移動與等待，不能只比較平面上的最短距離。","textEn":"Record long walking segments separately from elevator waits, comparing accessibility and arrival-time distributions across transfer routes. Travel time includes movement and waiting rather than plan distance alone.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-05-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨樓層轉乘時間」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Travel time between levels\" is correct?","options":["平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑","只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡","本單元將長距離步行與電梯等待分開記錄，對照不同轉乘路線的可達性和到達時間分布。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger.","An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope.","Record long walking segments separately from elevator waits, comparing accessibility and arrival-time distributions across transfer routes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元將長距離步行與電梯等待分開記錄，對照不同轉乘路線的可達性和到達時間分布。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Record long walking segments separately from elevator waits, comparing accessibility and arrival-time distributions across transfer routes. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":5},{"id":"b383-v16-06","title":"跨樓層轉乘時間：定量估算","titleEn":"Travel time between levels: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-05"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跨樓層轉乘時間」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Travel time between levels” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=120 m；假想步速 speed=0.8 m/s；等待時間 wait=35 s。公式 y=distance/speed+wait，代入得 y=185 s。邊界：定步速與固定等待的概念估算，未含煙氣、擁擠及協助需求分布。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: walking distance distance=120 m; assumed walking speed speed=0.8 m/s; waiting time wait=35 s. Formula y=distance/speed+wait gives y=185 s. Boundary: Constant speed and fixed waiting; smoke, crowd interaction and distribution of assistance needs are omitted. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：分段記錄行走與等待，不以最快受試者代表所有旅客，並對照不同能力群體。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record movement and waiting separately, avoid representing everyone by the fastest participant, and compare groups with different abilities.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-06-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=120 m；假想步速 speed=0.8 m/s；等待時間 wait=35 s。公式 y=distance/speed+wait，代入得 y=185 s。邊界：定步速與固定等待的概念估算，未含煙氣、擁擠及協助需求分布。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: walking distance distance=120 m; assumed walking speed speed=0.8 m/s; waiting time wait=35 s. Formula y=distance/speed+wait gives y=185 s. Boundary: Constant speed and fixed waiting; smoke, crowd interaction and distribution of assistance needs are omitted.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-06-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨樓層轉乘時間」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Travel time between levels\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=120 m；假想步速 speed=0.8 m/s；等待時間 wait=35 s。","平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度","電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: walking distance distance=120 m; assumed walking speed speed=0.8 m/s; waiting time wait=35 s.","A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant.","Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：行走距離 distance=120 m；假想步速 speed=0.8 m/s；等待時間 wait=35 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: walking distance distance=120 m; assumed walking speed speed=0.8 m/s; waiting time wait=35 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":6},{"id":"b383-v16-07","title":"跨樓層轉乘時間：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Travel time between levels: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-06"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跨樓層轉乘時間」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Travel time between levels” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"分段記錄行走與等待，不以最快受試者代表所有旅客，並對照不同能力群體。以「跨樓層轉乘時間」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record movement and waiting separately, avoid representing everyone by the fastest participant, and compare groups with different abilities. For travel time between levels, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把假想步速 speed 從 0.8 改成 0.88 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 185 變為 171.364 s。先說明「跨樓層轉乘時間」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only assumed walking speed speed from 0.8 to 0.88 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 185 to 171.364 s. Explain the causal direction for travel time between levels, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只量無人環境步行時間會低估轉乘負擔，電梯等待與路徑中斷可能主導總時間。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Uncrowded walking tests understate transfer burden when elevator waits or route interruptions dominate total time. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-07-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"分段記錄行走與等待，不以最快受試者代表所有旅客，並對照不同能力群體。以「跨樓層轉乘時間」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Record movement and waiting separately, avoid representing everyone by the fastest participant, and compare groups with different abilities. For travel time between levels, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-07-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把假想步速 speed 從 0.8 改成 0.88 m/s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 185 變為 171.364 s。先說明「跨樓層轉乘時間」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only assumed walking speed speed from 0.8 to 0.88 m/s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 185 to 171.364 s. Explain the causal direction for travel time between levels, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨樓層轉乘時間」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Travel time between levels\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","分段記錄行走與等待，不以最快受試者代表所有旅客，並對照不同能力群體。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Record movement and waiting separately, avoid representing everyone by the fastest participant, and compare groups with different abilities.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分段記錄行走與等待，不以最快受試者代表所有旅客，並對照不同能力群體。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record movement and waiting separately, avoid representing everyone by the fastest participant, and compare groups with different abilities. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":7},{"id":"b383-v16-08","title":"跨樓層轉乘時間：失效診斷","titleEn":"Travel time between levels: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-07"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跨樓層轉乘時間」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Travel time between levels” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量無人環境步行時間會低估轉乘負擔，電梯等待與路徑中斷可能主導總時間。回到「跨樓層轉乘時間」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Uncrowded walking tests understate transfer burden when elevator waits or route interruptions dominate total time. Trace the input chain for travel time between levels. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：定步速與固定等待的概念估算，未含煙氣、擁擠及協助需求分布。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant speed and fixed waiting; smoke, crowd interaction and distribution of assistance needs are omitted.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-08-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量無人環境步行時間會低估轉乘負擔，電梯等待與路徑中斷可能主導總時間。回到「跨樓層轉乘時間」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Uncrowded walking tests understate transfer burden when elevator waits or route interruptions dominate total time. Trace the input chain for travel time between levels. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-08-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨樓層轉乘時間」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Travel time between levels\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡","只量無人環境步行時間會低估轉乘負擔，電梯等待與路徑中斷可能主導總時間。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope.","Uncrowded walking tests understate transfer burden when elevator waits or route interruptions dominate total time."],"answer":2,"explanation":"只量無人環境步行時間會低估轉乘負擔，電梯等待與路徑中斷可能主導總時間。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Uncrowded walking tests understate transfer burden when elevator waits or route interruptions dominate total time. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":2,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":8}],"order":1},{"id":"b383-v16-s2","title":"高差與坡道路徑與扶梯下端積壓","titleEn":"Level changes and ramp routes & Accumulation at escalator landings","description":"本階段聚焦「高差與坡道路徑」與「扶梯下端積壓」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Level changes and ramp routes\" and \"Accumulation at escalator landings\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b383-v16-09","title":"高差與坡道路徑：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Level changes and ramp routes: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-08"],"objective":"說明「高差與坡道路徑」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level changes and ramp routes” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元用端點高程與水平距離檢查坡道幾何，另外保留平台、轉向空間與排水造成的局部橫坡。坡度以高差除以水平長度定義，不能把斜面長度直接當分母。平均坡度之外還要檢查平台、橫坡與轉折，因為輪椅使用者在坡道終端需要轉向與停止的空間；符合一個幾何比值並不代表整條無障礙路徑連續可用。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：幾何教學值，不宣告符合任何司法區的坡道上限。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「高差與坡道路徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Check ramp geometry using endpoint elevations and horizontal run, while separately retaining landings, turning space and drainage-related local cross-slope. Slope uses rise divided by horizontal run, not sloping surface length. Landings, cross-slope and transitions also matter because wheelchair users need space to turn and stop. Meeting one geometric ratio does not establish continuous usability of an accessible route. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Geometric teaching value, without asserting compliance with a jurisdictional ramp limit. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level changes and ramp routes” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：高差 rise=0.45 m；水平長度 run=7.5 m。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: vertical rise rise=0.45 m; horizontal run run=7.5 m.","failure":"常見誤解：「只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「高差與坡道路徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Level changes and ramp routes”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-09-k1","title":"高差與坡道路徑","titleEn":"Level changes and ramp routes","text":"本單元用端點高程與水平距離檢查坡道幾何，另外保留平台、轉向空間與排水造成的局部橫坡。坡度以高差除以水平長度定義，不能把斜面長度直接當分母。","textEn":"Check ramp geometry using endpoint elevations and horizontal run, while separately retaining landings, turning space and drainage-related local cross-slope. Slope uses rise divided by horizontal run, not sloping surface length.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-09-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「高差與坡道路徑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level changes and ramp routes\" is correct?","options":["本單元用端點高程與水平距離檢查坡道幾何，另外保留平台、轉向空間與排水造成的局部橫坡。","只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["Check ramp geometry using endpoint elevations and horizontal run, while separately retaining landings, turning space and drainage-related local cross-slope.","An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元用端點高程與水平距離檢查坡道幾何，另外保留平台、轉向空間與排水造成的局部橫坡。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Check ramp geometry using endpoint elevations and horizontal run, while separately retaining landings, turning space and drainage-related local cross-slope. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":9},{"id":"b383-v16-10","title":"高差與坡道路徑：定量估算","titleEn":"Level changes and ramp routes: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-09"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「高差與坡道路徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level changes and ramp routes” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：高差 rise=0.45 m；水平長度 run=7.5 m。公式 y=rise/run*100，代入得 y=6 percent。邊界：幾何教學值，不宣告符合任何司法區的坡道上限。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: vertical rise rise=0.45 m; horizontal run run=7.5 m. Formula y=rise/run*100 gives y=6 percent. Boundary: Geometric teaching value, without asserting compliance with a jurisdictional ramp limit. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一高程基準量端點，再沿行走路徑抽測局部坡度、橫坡與平台平整度。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Survey endpoints on one elevation datum, then sample local slope, cross-slope and landing level along the route.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-10-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：高差 rise=0.45 m；水平長度 run=7.5 m。公式 y=rise/run*100，代入得 y=6 percent。邊界：幾何教學值，不宣告符合任何司法區的坡道上限。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: vertical rise rise=0.45 m; horizontal run run=7.5 m. Formula y=rise/run*100 gives y=6 percent. Boundary: Geometric teaching value, without asserting compliance with a jurisdictional ramp limit.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-10-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「高差與坡道路徑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level changes and ramp routes\", which statement holds?","options":["整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠","原創假想教學輸入：高差 rise=0.45 m；水平長度 run=7.5 m。","照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口"],"optionsEn":["A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: vertical rise rise=0.45 m; horizontal run run=7.5 m.","Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：高差 rise=0.45 m；水平長度 run=7.5 m。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: vertical rise rise=0.45 m; horizontal run run=7.5 m. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":10},{"id":"b383-v16-11","title":"高差與坡道路徑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level changes and ramp routes: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-10"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「高差與坡道路徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Level changes and ramp routes” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一高程基準量端點，再沿行走路徑抽測局部坡度、橫坡與平台平整度。以「高差與坡道路徑」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Survey endpoints on one elevation datum, then sample local slope, cross-slope and landing level along the route. For level changes and ramp routes, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把水平長度 run 從 7.5 改成 8.25 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 6 變為 5.45455 percent。先說明「高差與坡道路徑」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only horizontal run run from 7.5 to 8.25 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 6 to 5.45455 percent. Explain the causal direction for level changes and ramp routes, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：兩端平均坡度合格仍可能隱藏短距離陡坡，排水沉陷又可能造成輪椅偏向。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: An acceptable endpoint average can hide a short steep segment, while drainage settlement can introduce a destabilizing cross-slope. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-11-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一高程基準量端點，再沿行走路徑抽測局部坡度、橫坡與平台平整度。以「高差與坡道路徑」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Survey endpoints on one elevation datum, then sample local slope, cross-slope and landing level along the route. For level changes and ramp routes, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-11-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把水平長度 run 從 7.5 改成 8.25 m（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 6 變為 5.45455 percent。先說明「高差與坡道路徑」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only horizontal run run from 7.5 to 8.25 m (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 6 to 5.45455 percent. Explain the causal direction for level changes and ramp routes, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「高差與坡道路徑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level changes and ramp routes\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","以同一高程基準量端點，再沿行走路徑抽測局部坡度、橫坡與平台平整度。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Survey endpoints on one elevation datum, then sample local slope, cross-slope and landing level along the route."],"answer":2,"explanation":"以同一高程基準量端點，再沿行走路徑抽測局部坡度、橫坡與平台平整度。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Survey endpoints on one elevation datum, then sample local slope, cross-slope and landing level along the route. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":11},{"id":"b383-v16-12","title":"高差與坡道路徑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level changes and ramp routes: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-11"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「高差與坡道路徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Level changes and ramp routes” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"兩端平均坡度合格仍可能隱藏短距離陡坡，排水沉陷又可能造成輪椅偏向。回到「高差與坡道路徑」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"An acceptable endpoint average can hide a short steep segment, while drainage settlement can introduce a destabilizing cross-slope. Trace the input chain for level changes and ramp routes. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：幾何教學值，不宣告符合任何司法區的坡道上限。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Geometric teaching value, without asserting compliance with a jurisdictional ramp limit.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-12-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"兩端平均坡度合格仍可能隱藏短距離陡坡，排水沉陷又可能造成輪椅偏向。回到「高差與坡道路徑」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"An acceptable endpoint average can hide a short steep segment, while drainage settlement can introduce a destabilizing cross-slope. Trace the input chain for level changes and ramp routes. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-12-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「高差與坡道路徑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level changes and ramp routes\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["兩端平均坡度合格仍可能隱藏短距離陡坡，排水沉陷又可能造成輪椅偏向。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable endpoint average can hide a short steep segment, while drainage settlement can introduce a destabilizing cross-slope.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":0,"explanation":"兩端平均坡度合格仍可能隱藏短距離陡坡，排水沉陷又可能造成輪椅偏向。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"An acceptable endpoint average can hide a short steep segment, while drainage settlement can introduce a destabilizing cross-slope. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":3,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":12},{"id":"b383-v16-13","title":"扶梯下端積壓：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Accumulation at escalator landings: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-12"],"objective":"說明「扶梯下端積壓」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Accumulation at escalator landings” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元追蹤下游突然降速造成的等候存量，避免只用扶梯運轉速度推論落地區可以承受人流。排隊人數依流入減流出的守恆關係累積。平均服務能力若只略高於平均需求，瞬間車潮仍會形成等待；人群不能被無限壓縮，所以排隊長度會回堵上游樓梯或月台，改變原先假設的到達方式。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「扶梯下端積壓」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Track waiting occupancy when downstream movement slows, avoiding inference of landing capacity from escalator running speed alone. A queue accumulates according to inflow minus outflow. Even service capacity slightly above mean demand can be overwhelmed by a train-arrival pulse. People cannot be compressed indefinitely, so a growing queue can block upstream stairs or platforms and alter the assumed arrival process. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Accumulation at escalator landings” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「扶梯下端積壓」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Accumulation at escalator landings”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-13-k1","title":"扶梯下端積壓","titleEn":"Accumulation at escalator landings","text":"本單元追蹤下游突然降速造成的等候存量，避免只用扶梯運轉速度推論落地區可以承受人流。排隊人數依流入減流出的守恆關係累積。","textEn":"Track waiting occupancy when downstream movement slows, avoiding inference of landing capacity from escalator running speed alone. A queue accumulates according to inflow minus outflow.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-13-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「扶梯下端積壓」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Accumulation at escalator landings\" is correct?","options":["出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊","本單元追蹤下游突然降速造成的等候存量，避免只用扶梯運轉速度推論落地區可以承受人流。","平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度"],"optionsEn":["Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.","Track waiting occupancy when downstream movement slows, avoiding inference of landing capacity from escalator running speed alone.","A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元追蹤下游突然降速造成的等候存量，避免只用扶梯運轉速度推論落地區可以承受人流。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Track waiting occupancy when downstream movement slows, avoiding inference of landing capacity from escalator running speed alone. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":13},{"id":"b383-v16-14","title":"扶梯下端積壓：定量估算","titleEn":"Accumulation at escalator landings: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-13"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「扶梯下端積壓」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Accumulation at escalator landings” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。公式 y=(arrival-service)*duration，代入得 y=72 persons。邊界：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s. Formula y=(arrival-service)*duration gives y=72 persons. Boundary: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-14-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。公式 y=(arrival-service)*duration，代入得 y=72 persons。邊界：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s. Formula y=(arrival-service)*duration gives y=72 persons. Boundary: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-14-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「扶梯下端積壓」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Accumulation at escalator landings\", which statement holds?","options":["電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s。"],"optionsEn":["Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：到達流率 arrival=3.2 persons/s；離開流率 service=2.6 persons/s；觀察時間 duration=120 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: arrival flow arrival=3.2 persons/s; departure flow service=2.6 persons/s; observation duration duration=120 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":14},{"id":"b383-v16-15","title":"扶梯下端積壓：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Accumulation at escalator landings: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-14"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「扶梯下端積壓」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Accumulation at escalator landings” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。以「扶梯下端積壓」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation. For accumulation at escalator landings, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把觀察時間 duration 從 120 改成 132 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 72 變為 79.2 persons。先說明「扶梯下端積壓」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only observation duration duration from 120 to 132 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 72 to 79.2 persons. Explain the causal direction for accumulation at escalator landings, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-15-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。以「扶梯下端積壓」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation. For accumulation at escalator landings, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-15-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把觀察時間 duration 從 120 改成 132 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 72 變為 79.2 persons。先說明「扶梯下端積壓」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only observation duration duration from 120 to 132 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 72 to 79.2 persons. Explain the causal direction for accumulation at escalator landings, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「扶梯下端積壓」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Accumulation at escalator landings\"?","options":["同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加"],"optionsEn":["Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時數進入、離開與區內存量，以影像匿名計數或人工抽樣核對人數守恆。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Count entries, exits and occupancy together, using anonymous image counts or manual samples to verify conservation. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":15},{"id":"b383-v16-16","title":"扶梯下端積壓：失效診斷","titleEn":"Accumulation at escalator landings: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-15"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「扶梯下端積壓」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Accumulation at escalator landings” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。回到「扶梯下端積壓」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. Trace the input chain for accumulation at escalator landings. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：固定流率、初始無排隊且流入大於流出；不含放棄、繞行及密度回饋。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Constant flows, initially empty queue and inflow above outflow; abandonment, rerouting and density feedback are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-16-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。回到「扶梯下端積壓」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. Trace the input chain for accumulation at escalator landings. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-16-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「扶梯下端積壓」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Accumulation at escalator landings\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。","平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows.","A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只量出口通過量會看不到後方累積，感測器漏計還可能讓看似平衡的流率掩蓋真實回堵。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Exit throughput alone misses upstream accumulation; missed detections can hide real spillback behind apparently balanced flows. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":4,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":16}],"order":2},{"id":"b383-v16-s3","title":"電梯等候平均存量與轉角匯流局部密度","titleEn":"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting & Local density at merging corners","description":"本階段聚焦「電梯等候平均存量」與「轉角匯流局部密度」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting\" and \"Local density at merging corners\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b383-v16-17","title":"電梯等候平均存量：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-16"],"objective":"說明「電梯等候平均存量」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Mean occupancy in elevator waiting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元以共同入口邊界核對平均等待與排隊人數，將乘車時間和候梯時間分開避免重複計入。穩態平均存量等於平均到達率乘平均停留時間，這是流量與庫存的連結，不需要先指定排隊分布。它不能描述單一尖峰時刻，也不會告訴人群在空間上如何分布；量測窗若仍在快速累積，就不宜直接套用穩態關係。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：穩態同一人群與同一系統邊界的長時間平均。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「電梯等候平均存量」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use one entrance boundary to compare average wait with queue size, separating travel inside the lift from waiting to avoid double counting. Mean occupancy equals mean arrival rate times mean residence time in steady flow. This connects throughput and inventory without requiring a specific queue distribution. It does not describe one peak instant or spatial distribution, and a rapidly accumulating observation window does not satisfy the steady-state interpretation. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Long-run averages of the same population within one steady system boundary. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Mean occupancy in elevator waiting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：平均到達率 arrival=2 persons/s；平均停留時間 waiting=45 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean arrival rate arrival=2 persons/s; mean residence time waiting=45 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「電梯等候平均存量」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Mean occupancy in elevator waiting”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-17-k1","title":"電梯等候平均存量","titleEn":"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting","text":"本單元以共同入口邊界核對平均等待與排隊人數，將乘車時間和候梯時間分開避免重複計入。穩態平均存量等於平均到達率乘平均停留時間，這是流量與庫存的連結，不需要先指定排隊分布。","textEn":"Use one entrance boundary to compare average wait with queue size, separating travel inside the lift from waiting to avoid double counting. Mean occupancy equals mean arrival rate times mean residence time in steady flow.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-17-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電梯等候平均存量」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting\" is correct?","options":["平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度","整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠","本單元以共同入口邊界核對平均等待與排隊人數，將乘車時間和候梯時間分開避免重複計入。"],"optionsEn":["A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant.","A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.","Use one entrance boundary to compare average wait with queue size, separating travel inside the lift from waiting to avoid double counting."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元以共同入口邊界核對平均等待與排隊人數，將乘車時間和候梯時間分開避免重複計入。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use one entrance boundary to compare average wait with queue size, separating travel inside the lift from waiting to avoid double counting. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":17},{"id":"b383-v16-18","title":"電梯等候平均存量：定量估算","titleEn":"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-17"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電梯等候平均存量」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Mean occupancy in elevator waiting” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：平均到達率 arrival=2 persons/s；平均停留時間 waiting=45 s。公式 y=arrival*waiting，代入得 y=90 persons。邊界：穩態同一人群與同一系統邊界的長時間平均。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean arrival rate arrival=2 persons/s; mean residence time waiting=45 s. Formula y=arrival*waiting gives y=90 persons. Boundary: Long-run averages of the same population within one steady system boundary. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：使用一致進出邊界估計流率與停留時間，並與獨立區內人數平均值比對。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Estimate flow and residence time using consistent boundaries and compare with an independent mean occupancy count.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-18-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：平均到達率 arrival=2 persons/s；平均停留時間 waiting=45 s。公式 y=arrival*waiting，代入得 y=90 persons。邊界：穩態同一人群與同一系統邊界的長時間平均。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean arrival rate arrival=2 persons/s; mean residence time waiting=45 s. Formula y=arrival*waiting gives y=90 persons. Boundary: Long-run averages of the same population within one steady system boundary.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-18-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電梯等候平均存量」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：平均到達率 arrival=2 persons/s；平均停留時間 waiting=45 s。","照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean arrival rate arrival=2 persons/s; mean residence time waiting=45 s.","Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：平均到達率 arrival=2 persons/s；平均停留時間 waiting=45 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: mean arrival rate arrival=2 persons/s; mean residence time waiting=45 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":18},{"id":"b383-v16-19","title":"電梯等候平均存量：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-18"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「電梯等候平均存量」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Mean occupancy in elevator waiting” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"使用一致進出邊界估計流率與停留時間，並與獨立區內人數平均值比對。以「電梯等候平均存量」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Estimate flow and residence time using consistent boundaries and compare with an independent mean occupancy count. For mean occupancy in elevator waiting, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把平均停留時間 waiting 從 45 改成 49.5 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 90 變為 99 persons。先說明「電梯等候平均存量」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only mean residence time waiting from 45 to 49.5 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 90 to 99 persons. Explain the causal direction for mean occupancy in elevator waiting, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：把包含站外等待的停留時間乘上站內流率會混用邊界，造成存量高估或低估。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Combining residence time that includes an outside queue with an inside flow rate mixes boundaries and biases occupancy. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-19-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"使用一致進出邊界估計流率與停留時間，並與獨立區內人數平均值比對。以「電梯等候平均存量」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Estimate flow and residence time using consistent boundaries and compare with an independent mean occupancy count. For mean occupancy in elevator waiting, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-19-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把平均停留時間 waiting 從 45 改成 49.5 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 90 變為 99 persons。先說明「電梯等候平均存量」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only mean residence time waiting from 45 to 49.5 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 90 to 99 persons. Explain the causal direction for mean occupancy in elevator waiting, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電梯等候平均存量」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting\"?","options":["允收準則可以等看到量測數據後再決定。","使用一致進出邊界估計流率與停留時間，並與獨立區內人數平均值比對。","平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑"],"optionsEn":["Acceptance criteria can be decided after the measured data have been seen.","Estimate flow and residence time using consistent boundaries and compare with an independent mean occupancy count.","The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger."],"answer":1,"explanation":"使用一致進出邊界估計流率與停留時間，並與獨立區內人數平均值比對。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Estimate flow and residence time using consistent boundaries and compare with an independent mean occupancy count. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":19},{"id":"b383-v16-20","title":"電梯等候平均存量：失效診斷","titleEn":"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-19"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電梯等候平均存量」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Mean occupancy in elevator waiting” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"把包含站外等待的停留時間乘上站內流率會混用邊界，造成存量高估或低估。回到「電梯等候平均存量」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Combining residence time that includes an outside queue with an inside flow rate mixes boundaries and biases occupancy. Trace the input chain for mean occupancy in elevator waiting. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：穩態同一人群與同一系統邊界的長時間平均。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Long-run averages of the same population within one steady system boundary.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-20-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"把包含站外等待的停留時間乘上站內流率會混用邊界，造成存量高估或低估。回到「電梯等候平均存量」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Combining residence time that includes an outside queue with an inside flow rate mixes boundaries and biases occupancy. Trace the input chain for mean occupancy in elevator waiting. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-20-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電梯等候平均存量」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Mean occupancy in elevator waiting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["症狀相同就代表原因相同，不必用量測區分。","整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠","把包含站外等待的停留時間乘上站內流率會混用邊界，造成存量高估或低估。"],"optionsEn":["Identical symptoms always mean identical causes, so no discriminating measurement is needed.","A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.","Combining residence time that includes an outside queue with an inside flow rate mixes boundaries and biases occupancy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"把包含站外等待的停留時間乘上站內流率會混用邊界，造成存量高估或低估。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Combining residence time that includes an outside queue with an inside flow rate mixes boundaries and biases occupancy. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":5,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":20},{"id":"b383-v16-21","title":"轉角匯流局部密度：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Local density at merging corners: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-20"],"objective":"說明「轉角匯流局部密度」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Local density at merging corners” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元觀察轉角、立柱與路徑交叉形成的群聚，對照同面積卻不同幾何配置的密度分布。平均密度是人數除以可用面積，設備、柱體與危險邊緣應從面積中扣除。相同平均密度可以包含完全不同的局部群聚；門口、扶梯出口與轉角的局部高密度，常比整個大廳平均值更能解釋行走速度下降。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：靜態平均密度，不是擠壓力或個別人的安全風險模型。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「轉角匯流局部密度」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Observe clustering at corners, columns and crossing paths, comparing density distributions for equal areas with different geometry. Mean density divides people by usable area after excluding equipment, columns and unsafe edges. The same average can conceal very different local clustering. High density at doors, escalator landings or corners often explains reduced walking speed better than the average across a large concourse. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Static mean density, not a crowd-pressure or individual-risk model. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Local density at merging corners” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：區內人數 people=180 persons；可站立面積 area=90 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupants people=180 persons; usable standing area area=90 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「轉角匯流局部密度」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Local density at merging corners”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-21-k1","title":"轉角匯流局部密度","titleEn":"Local density at merging corners","text":"本單元觀察轉角、立柱與路徑交叉形成的群聚，對照同面積卻不同幾何配置的密度分布。平均密度是人數除以可用面積，設備、柱體與危險邊緣應從面積中扣除。","textEn":"Observe clustering at corners, columns and crossing paths, comparing density distributions for equal areas with different geometry. Mean density divides people by usable area after excluding equipment, columns and unsafe edges.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-21-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「轉角匯流局部密度」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Local density at merging corners\" is correct?","options":["本單元觀察轉角、立柱與路徑交叉形成的群聚，對照同面積卻不同幾何配置的密度分布。","整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠","電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數"],"optionsEn":["Observe clustering at corners, columns and crossing paths, comparing density distributions for equal areas with different geometry.","A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.","Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元觀察轉角、立柱與路徑交叉形成的群聚，對照同面積卻不同幾何配置的密度分布。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Observe clustering at corners, columns and crossing paths, comparing density distributions for equal areas with different geometry. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":21},{"id":"b383-v16-22","title":"轉角匯流局部密度：定量估算","titleEn":"Local density at merging corners: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-21"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「轉角匯流局部密度」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Local density at merging corners” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：區內人數 people=180 persons；可站立面積 area=90 m2。公式 y=people/area，代入得 y=2 persons/m2。邊界：靜態平均密度，不是擠壓力或個別人的安全風險模型。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupants people=180 persons; usable standing area area=90 m2. Formula y=people/area gives y=2 persons/m2. Boundary: Static mean density, not a crowd-pressure or individual-risk model. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：用網格分區計數比較平均與局部尖峰，記錄可用面積隨設備或圍籬變動的情況。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Count occupants in spatial cells, compare mean and local peaks, and record changes in usable area from equipment or barriers.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-22-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：區內人數 people=180 persons；可站立面積 area=90 m2。公式 y=people/area，代入得 y=2 persons/m2。邊界：靜態平均密度，不是擠壓力或個別人的安全風險模型。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupants people=180 persons; usable standing area area=90 m2. Formula y=people/area gives y=2 persons/m2. Boundary: Static mean density, not a crowd-pressure or individual-risk model.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-22-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「轉角匯流局部密度」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Local density at merging corners\", which statement holds?","options":["測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","原創假想教學輸入：區內人數 people=180 persons；可站立面積 area=90 m2。","兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加"],"optionsEn":["One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupants people=180 persons; usable standing area area=90 m2.","Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：區內人數 people=180 persons；可站立面積 area=90 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: occupants people=180 persons; usable standing area area=90 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":22},{"id":"b383-v16-23","title":"轉角匯流局部密度：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Local density at merging corners: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-22"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「轉角匯流局部密度」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Local density at merging corners” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"用網格分區計數比較平均與局部尖峰，記錄可用面積隨設備或圍籬變動的情況。以「轉角匯流局部密度」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Count occupants in spatial cells, compare mean and local peaks, and record changes in usable area from equipment or barriers. For local density at merging corners, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把可站立面積 area 從 90 改成 99 m2（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 2 變為 1.81818 persons/m2。先說明「轉角匯流局部密度」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only usable standing area area from 90 to 99 m2 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 2 to 1.81818 persons/m2. Explain the causal direction for local density at merging corners, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：將封閉區域算入面積會低估密度，遮蔽導致漏計又可能恰好發生在最擁擠的地方。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Including closed areas understates density; occlusion-related undercounting can be worst precisely where crowding is greatest. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-23-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"用網格分區計數比較平均與局部尖峰，記錄可用面積隨設備或圍籬變動的情況。以「轉角匯流局部密度」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Count occupants in spatial cells, compare mean and local peaks, and record changes in usable area from equipment or barriers. For local density at merging corners, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-23-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把可站立面積 area 從 90 改成 99 m2（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 2 變為 1.81818 persons/m2。先說明「轉角匯流局部密度」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only usable standing area area from 90 to 99 m2 (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 2 to 1.81818 persons/m2. Explain the causal direction for local density at merging corners, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「轉角匯流局部密度」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Local density at merging corners\"?","options":["只要結構分析模型看起來合理，就可以省略現場量測與試驗。","只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡","用網格分區計數比較平均與局部尖峰，記錄可用面積隨設備或圍籬變動的情況。"],"optionsEn":["If the structural model looks reasonable, site measurement and testing can be skipped.","An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope.","Count occupants in spatial cells, compare mean and local peaks, and record changes in usable area from equipment or barriers."],"answer":2,"explanation":"用網格分區計數比較平均與局部尖峰，記錄可用面積隨設備或圍籬變動的情況。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Count occupants in spatial cells, compare mean and local peaks, and record changes in usable area from equipment or barriers. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":23},{"id":"b383-v16-24","title":"轉角匯流局部密度：失效診斷","titleEn":"Local density at merging corners: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-23"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「轉角匯流局部密度」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Local density at merging corners” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"將封閉區域算入面積會低估密度，遮蔽導致漏計又可能恰好發生在最擁擠的地方。回到「轉角匯流局部密度」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Including closed areas understates density; occlusion-related undercounting can be worst precisely where crowding is greatest. Trace the input chain for local density at merging corners. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：靜態平均密度，不是擠壓力或個別人的安全風險模型。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Static mean density, not a crowd-pressure or individual-risk model.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-24-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"將封閉區域算入面積會低估密度，遮蔽導致漏計又可能恰好發生在最擁擠的地方。回到「轉角匯流局部密度」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Including closed areas understates density; occlusion-related undercounting can be worst precisely where crowding is greatest. Trace the input chain for local density at merging corners. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-24-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「轉角匯流局部密度」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Local density at merging corners\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["將封閉區域算入面積會低估密度，遮蔽導致漏計又可能恰好發生在最擁擠的地方。","只要結構還沒倒，就代表安全餘裕仍然足夠。","電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數"],"optionsEn":["Including closed areas understates density; occlusion-related undercounting can be worst precisely where crowding is greatest.","As long as the structure is still standing, its safety margin must still be adequate.","Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"將封閉區域算入面積會低估密度，遮蔽導致漏計又可能恰好發生在最擁擠的地方。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Including closed areas understates density; occlusion-related undercounting can be worst precisely where crowding is greatest. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":6,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":24}],"order":3},{"id":"b383-v16-s4","title":"垂直運輸往返節拍與層間辨識與照明","titleEn":"Round-trip vertical-service cycle & Level identification and lighting","description":"本階段聚焦「垂直運輸往返節拍」與「層間辨識與照明」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Round-trip vertical-service cycle\" and \"Level identification and lighting\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b383-v16-25","title":"垂直運輸往返節拍：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Round-trip vertical-service cycle: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-24"],"objective":"說明「垂直運輸往返節拍」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Round-trip vertical-service cycle” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元把電梯登乘、行進、離開及回程直接列成完整週期，將門動作納入服務時間並區分每小時循環與每小時旅客數。單台電梯往返週期由登乘、行進、離開及回程組成，門動作必須被計入服務階段。理想每小時循環數不等於每小時可服務人數，還需考慮載客量、樓層呼叫、上下行需求與可用性；乘客集中到達時，平均循環有餘裕也可能形成長候梯隊伍。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩樓層串行往返且無中途停靠的理想循環，未含載客量及等待分布。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「垂直運輸往返節拍」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"List elevator boarding, travel, alighting and return directly as one complete cycle, including door actions and distinguishing trips per hour from passengers per hour. An elevator round trip includes boarding, travel, alighting and return, with door actions included in the service phases. Ideal cycles per hour are not passengers per hour: occupancy, floor calls, directional demand and availability also matter. Concentrated passenger arrivals can create long waits even when the mean cycle appears to offer spare capacity. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Ideal serial round trip between two levels without intermediate stops, excluding occupancy and waiting distributions. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Round-trip vertical-service cycle” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：開門登乘及關門 board=18 s；載客行進 travel=24 s；開門離開及關門 alight=16 s；回程時間 return_=24 s。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: door and boarding time board=18 s; loaded travel travel=24 s; door and alighting time alight=16 s; return travel return_=24 s.","failure":"常見誤解：「電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「垂直運輸往返節拍」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Round-trip vertical-service cycle”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-25-k1","title":"垂直運輸往返節拍","titleEn":"Round-trip vertical-service cycle","text":"本單元把電梯登乘、行進、離開及回程直接列成完整週期，將門動作納入服務時間並區分每小時循環與每小時旅客數。單台電梯往返週期由登乘、行進、離開及回程組成，門動作必須被計入服務階段。","textEn":"List elevator boarding, travel, alighting and return directly as one complete cycle, including door actions and distinguishing trips per hour from passengers per hour. An elevator round trip includes boarding, travel, alighting and return, with door actions included in the service phases.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-25-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「垂直運輸往返節拍」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Round-trip vertical-service cycle\" is correct?","options":["電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數","本單元把電梯登乘、行進、離開及回程直接列成完整週期，將門動作納入服務時間並區分每小時循環與每小時旅客數。","照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口"],"optionsEn":["Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour.","List elevator boarding, travel, alighting and return directly as one complete cycle, including door actions and distinguishing trips per hour from passengers per hour.","Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元把電梯登乘、行進、離開及回程直接列成完整週期，將門動作納入服務時間並區分每小時循環與每小時旅客數。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"List elevator boarding, travel, alighting and return directly as one complete cycle, including door actions and distinguishing trips per hour from passengers per hour. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":25},{"id":"b383-v16-26","title":"垂直運輸往返節拍：定量估算","titleEn":"Round-trip vertical-service cycle: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-25"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「垂直運輸往返節拍」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Round-trip vertical-service cycle” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：開門登乘及關門 board=18 s；載客行進 travel=24 s；開門離開及關門 alight=16 s；回程時間 return_=24 s。公式 y=3600/(board+travel+alight+return_)，代入得 y=43.9024 trips/h。邊界：兩樓層串行往返且無中途停靠的理想循環，未含載客量及等待分布。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: door and boarding time board=18 s; loaded travel travel=24 s; door and alighting time alight=16 s; return travel return_=24 s. Formula y=3600/(board+travel+alight+return_) gives y=43.9024 trips/h. Boundary: Ideal serial round trip between two levels without intermediate stops, excluding occupancy and waiting distributions. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以同一門開關事件界定各階段，分別記錄登乘與離開，抽查回程空載及途中呼叫是否改變循環邊界。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Define stages with consistent door events, record boarding and alighting separately, and inspect whether empty return or intermediate calls change the cycle boundary.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-26-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：開門登乘及關門 board=18 s；載客行進 travel=24 s；開門離開及關門 alight=16 s；回程時間 return_=24 s。公式 y=3600/(board+travel+alight+return_)，代入得 y=43.9024 trips/h。邊界：兩樓層串行往返且無中途停靠的理想循環，未含載客量及等待分布。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: door and boarding time board=18 s; loaded travel travel=24 s; door and alighting time alight=16 s; return travel return_=24 s. Formula y=3600/(board+travel+alight+return_) gives y=43.9024 trips/h. Boundary: Ideal serial round trip between two levels without intermediate stops, excluding occupancy and waiting distributions.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-26-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「垂直運輸往返節拍」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Round-trip vertical-service cycle\", which statement holds?","options":["所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑","原創假想教學輸入：開門登乘及關門 board=18 s。"],"optionsEn":["All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: door and boarding time board=18 s."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：開門登乘及關門 board=18 s；載客行進 travel=24 s；開門離開及關門 alight=16 s；回程時間 return_=24 s。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: door and boarding time board=18 s; loaded travel travel=24 s; door and alighting time alight=16 s; return travel return_=24 s. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":26},{"id":"b383-v16-27","title":"垂直運輸往返節拍：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Round-trip vertical-service cycle: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-26"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「垂直運輸往返節拍」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Round-trip vertical-service cycle” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以同一門開關事件界定各階段，分別記錄登乘與離開，抽查回程空載及途中呼叫是否改變循環邊界。以「垂直運輸往返節拍」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Define stages with consistent door events, record boarding and alighting separately, and inspect whether empty return or intermediate calls change the cycle boundary. For round-trip vertical-service cycle, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把開門登乘及關門 board 從 18 改成 19.8 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 43.9024 變為 42.9594 trips/h。先說明「垂直運輸往返節拍」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only door and boarding time board from 18 to 19.8 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 43.9024 to 42.9594 trips/h. Explain the causal direction for round-trip vertical-service cycle, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：漏算回程會高估循環率，把門動作在兩個階段重複計入則會低估能力；實際載客需求還可能由上游排隊控制。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitting return overstates cycle rate, while counting door motion twice understates capacity; actual passenger demand may also be governed by upstream queues. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-27-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以同一門開關事件界定各階段，分別記錄登乘與離開，抽查回程空載及途中呼叫是否改變循環邊界。以「垂直運輸往返節拍」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Define stages with consistent door events, record boarding and alighting separately, and inspect whether empty return or intermediate calls change the cycle boundary. For round-trip vertical-service cycle, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-27-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把開門登乘及關門 board 從 18 改成 19.8 s（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 43.9024 變為 42.9594 trips/h。先說明「垂直運輸往返節拍」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only door and boarding time board from 18 to 19.8 s (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 43.9024 to 42.9594 trips/h. Explain the causal direction for round-trip vertical-service cycle, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「垂直運輸往返節拍」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Round-trip vertical-service cycle\"?","options":["以同一門開關事件界定各階段，分別記錄登乘與離開，抽查回程空載及途中呼叫是否改變循環邊界。","量測時不必記錄溫度、速度、運行歷程與施工荷重，因為它們不會影響結果。","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["Define stages with consistent door events, record boarding and alighting separately, and inspect whether empty return or intermediate calls change the cycle boundary.","Temperature, speed, operating history and construction loads need not be recorded because they cannot affect the result.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":0,"explanation":"以同一門開關事件界定各階段，分別記錄登乘與離開，抽查回程空載及途中呼叫是否改變循環邊界。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Define stages with consistent door events, record boarding and alighting separately, and inspect whether empty return or intermediate calls change the cycle boundary. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":27},{"id":"b383-v16-28","title":"垂直運輸往返節拍：失效診斷","titleEn":"Round-trip vertical-service cycle: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-27"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「垂直運輸往返節拍」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Round-trip vertical-service cycle” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"漏算回程會高估循環率，把門動作在兩個階段重複計入則會低估能力；實際載客需求還可能由上游排隊控制。回到「垂直運輸往返節拍」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitting return overstates cycle rate, while counting door motion twice understates capacity; actual passenger demand may also be governed by upstream queues. Trace the input chain for round-trip vertical-service cycle. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：兩樓層串行往返且無中途停靠的理想循環，未含載客量及等待分布。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Ideal serial round trip between two levels without intermediate stops, excluding occupancy and waiting distributions.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-28-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"漏算回程會高估循環率，把門動作在兩個階段重複計入則會低估能力；實際載客需求還可能由上游排隊控制。回到「垂直運輸往返節拍」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Omitting return overstates cycle rate, while counting door motion twice understates capacity; actual passenger demand may also be governed by upstream queues. Trace the input chain for round-trip vertical-service cycle. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-28-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「垂直運輸往返節拍」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Round-trip vertical-service cycle\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["所有異常都來自施工人員失誤，設計與細部不需要檢討。","漏算回程會高估循環率，把門動作在兩個階段重複計入則會低估能力；實際載客需求還可能由上游排隊控制。","照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口"],"optionsEn":["Every anomaly is a workmanship error, so design and detailing never need review.","Omitting return overstates cycle rate, while counting door motion twice understates capacity; actual passenger demand may also be governed by upstream queues.","Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner."],"answer":1,"explanation":"漏算回程會高估循環率，把門動作在兩個階段重複計入則會低估能力；實際載客需求還可能由上游排隊控制。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitting return overstates cycle rate, while counting door motion twice understates capacity; actual passenger demand may also be governed by upstream queues. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":7,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":28},{"id":"b383-v16-29","title":"層間辨識與照明：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Level identification and lighting: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-28"],"objective":"說明「層間辨識與照明」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Level identification and lighting” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元檢查轉折處照度與指標對比，讓旅客能在到達分流點前辨認正確樓層與方向。平均照度由到達工作面的光通量除以面積估算，但光學分布決定暗點是否存在。煙氣、污損與電池老化可能同時降低可見性；指示方向、對比與旅客視力也會影響辨識，不能只用燈具是否亮著作為完成檢核。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻平均照度估算，未模擬煙氣散射或法定最低照度。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「層間辨識與照明」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Check illuminance and sign contrast at turns so travellers can identify the correct level and direction before reaching the route split. Mean illuminance divides useful luminous flux by area, but optical distribution determines dark spots. Smoke, dirt and battery ageing can reduce visibility together. Directional cues, contrast and eyesight affect recognition, so a lamp being on is not a complete verification. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform mean-illuminance estimate without smoke scattering or statutory minimum values. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Level identification and lighting” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：光通量 flux=2400 lm；利用係數 util=0.45 1；受照面積 area=24 m2。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: luminous flux flux=2400 lm; utilization factor util=0.45 1; illuminated area area=24 m2.","failure":"常見誤解：「照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「層間辨識與照明」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Level identification and lighting”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-29-k1","title":"層間辨識與照明","titleEn":"Level identification and lighting","text":"本單元檢查轉折處照度與指標對比，讓旅客能在到達分流點前辨認正確樓層與方向。平均照度由到達工作面的光通量除以面積估算，但光學分布決定暗點是否存在。","textEn":"Check illuminance and sign contrast at turns so travellers can identify the correct level and direction before reaching the route split. Mean illuminance divides useful luminous flux by area, but optical distribution determines dark spots.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-29-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「層間辨識與照明」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Level identification and lighting\" is correct?","options":["照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","本單元檢查轉折處照度與指標對比，讓旅客能在到達分流點前辨認正確樓層與方向。"],"optionsEn":["Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Check illuminance and sign contrast at turns so travellers can identify the correct level and direction before reaching the route split."],"answer":2,"explanation":"本單元檢查轉折處照度與指標對比，讓旅客能在到達分流點前辨認正確樓層與方向。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Check illuminance and sign contrast at turns so travellers can identify the correct level and direction before reaching the route split. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":29},{"id":"b383-v16-30","title":"層間辨識與照明：定量估算","titleEn":"Level identification and lighting: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-29"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「層間辨識與照明」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Level identification and lighting” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：光通量 flux=2400 lm；利用係數 util=0.45 1；受照面積 area=24 m2。公式 y=flux*util/area，代入得 y=45 lx。邊界：均勻平均照度估算，未模擬煙氣散射或法定最低照度。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: luminous flux flux=2400 lm; utilization factor util=0.45 1; illuminated area area=24 m2. Formula y=flux*util/area gives y=45 lx. Boundary: Uniform mean-illuminance estimate without smoke scattering or statutory minimum values. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：以網格量測平面照度並尋找最低點，對照電池放電前後與不同觀看方向。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Measure illuminance on a grid, identify minima, and compare before/after battery discharge and different viewing directions.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-30-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：光通量 flux=2400 lm；利用係數 util=0.45 1；受照面積 area=24 m2。公式 y=flux*util/area，代入得 y=45 lx。邊界：均勻平均照度估算，未模擬煙氣散射或法定最低照度。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: luminous flux flux=2400 lm; utilization factor util=0.45 1; illuminated area area=24 m2. Formula y=flux*util/area gives y=45 lx. Boundary: Uniform mean-illuminance estimate without smoke scattering or statutory minimum values.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-30-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「層間辨識與照明」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Level identification and lighting\", which statement holds?","options":["原創假想教學輸入：光通量 flux=2400 lm；利用係數 util=0.45 1；受照面積 area=24 m2。","兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加","只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡"],"optionsEn":["Original hypothetical teaching inputs: luminous flux flux=2400 lm; utilization factor util=0.45 1; illuminated area area=24 m2.","Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity.","An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope."],"answer":0,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：光通量 flux=2400 lm；利用係數 util=0.45 1；受照面積 area=24 m2。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: luminous flux flux=2400 lm; utilization factor util=0.45 1; illuminated area area=24 m2. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":30},{"id":"b383-v16-31","title":"層間辨識與照明：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Level identification and lighting: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-30"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「層間辨識與照明」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Level identification and lighting” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"以網格量測平面照度並尋找最低點，對照電池放電前後與不同觀看方向。以「層間辨識與照明」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Measure illuminance on a grid, identify minima, and compare before/after battery discharge and different viewing directions. For level identification and lighting, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把光通量 flux 從 2400 改成 2640 lm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 45 變為 49.5 lx。先說明「層間辨識與照明」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only luminous flux flux from 2400 to 2640 lm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 45 to 49.5 lx. Explain the causal direction for level identification and lighting, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：亮度集中在燈具下方可能留下暗區，指示牌反光也可降低遠距離的有效對比。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Light concentrated beneath fixtures leaves dark regions; sign glare can also reduce effective contrast at a distance. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-31-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"以網格量測平面照度並尋找最低點，對照電池放電前後與不同觀看方向。以「層間辨識與照明」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Measure illuminance on a grid, identify minima, and compare before/after battery discharge and different viewing directions. For level identification and lighting, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-31-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把光通量 flux 從 2400 改成 2640 lm（增加百分之十），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 45 變為 49.5 lx。先說明「層間辨識與照明」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only luminous flux flux from 2400 to 2640 lm (increase by ten percent), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 45 to 49.5 lx. Explain the causal direction for level identification and lighting, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「層間辨識與照明」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Level identification and lighting\"?","options":["沿用另一處鐵路設施或路線的量測結果，就可視為本工程已完成驗證。","以網格量測平面照度並尋找最低點，對照電池放電前後與不同觀看方向。","平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度"],"optionsEn":["Reusing results from another railway facility or route counts as verifying this structure.","Measure illuminance on a grid, identify minima, and compare before/after battery discharge and different viewing directions.","A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant."],"answer":1,"explanation":"以網格量測平面照度並尋找最低點，對照電池放電前後與不同觀看方向。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Measure illuminance on a grid, identify minima, and compare before/after battery discharge and different viewing directions. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":31},{"id":"b383-v16-32","title":"層間辨識與照明：失效診斷","titleEn":"Level identification and lighting: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-31"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「層間辨識與照明」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Level identification and lighting” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"亮度集中在燈具下方可能留下暗區，指示牌反光也可降低遠距離的有效對比。回到「層間辨識與照明」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Light concentrated beneath fixtures leaves dark regions; sign glare can also reduce effective contrast at a distance. Trace the input chain for level identification and lighting. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：均勻平均照度估算，未模擬煙氣散射或法定最低照度。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Uniform mean-illuminance estimate without smoke scattering or statutory minimum values.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「照明平均值足夠就保證所有角落都能清楚辨識出口」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"Adequate mean lighting guarantees clear exit recognition at every corner.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-32-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"亮度集中在燈具下方可能留下暗區，指示牌反光也可降低遠距離的有效對比。回到「層間辨識與照明」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Light concentrated beneath fixtures leaves dark regions; sign glare can also reduce effective contrast at a distance. Trace the input chain for level identification and lighting. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-32-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「層間辨識與照明」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Level identification and lighting\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["補一層塗料或放寬允收值，就能解決大多數劣化問題。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","亮度集中在燈具下方可能留下暗區，指示牌反光也可降低遠距離的有效對比。"],"optionsEn":["Adding a coat of paint or widening the acceptance limits solves most deterioration problems.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","Light concentrated beneath fixtures leaves dark regions; sign glare can also reduce effective contrast at a distance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"亮度集中在燈具下方可能留下暗區，指示牌反光也可降低遠距離的有效對比。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Light concentrated beneath fixtures leaves dark regions; sign glare can also reduce effective contrast at a distance. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":8,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":32}],"order":4},{"id":"b383-v16-s5","title":"電梯停用替代路徑與跨層動線驗證安排","titleEn":"Alternative routes during lift outages & Planning multilevel route verification","description":"本階段聚焦「電梯停用替代路徑」與「跨層動線驗證安排」：先建立機制、系統路徑與定量模型，再設計試驗驗證並診斷失效。","descriptionEn":"This stage covers \"Alternative routes during lift outages\" and \"Planning multilevel route verification\": establish the mechanism, system paths and quantitative model first, then design verification and diagnose failures.","steps":[{"id":"b383-v16-33","title":"電梯停用替代路徑：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Alternative routes during lift outages: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-32"],"objective":"說明「電梯停用替代路徑」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Alternative routes during lift outages” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元以角色任務矩陣檢查電梯停用後的可達路徑，不能把需要樓梯的替代線視為所有旅客可用。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。需求、狀態、轉移與危害各有不同分母，執行很多正常案例仍可能漏掉罕見但重要的交接；同一案例重跑多次不會自動增加獨立需求的覆蓋。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「電梯停用替代路徑」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Use a user-task matrix to examine accessible routes during a lift outage; a stair-only alternative is not usable by every passenger. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator. Requirements, states, transitions and hazards have different denominators. Many normal cases can still omit a rare but important handoff, and repeating one case does not automatically cover additional independent requirements. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Alternative routes during lift outages” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","failure":"常見誤解：「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「電梯停用替代路徑」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Alternative routes during lift outages”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-33-k1","title":"電梯停用替代路徑","titleEn":"Alternative routes during lift outages","text":"本單元以角色任務矩陣檢查電梯停用後的可達路徑，不能把需要樓梯的替代線視為所有旅客可用。測試覆蓋率只對已定義的分母有意義。","textEn":"Use a user-task matrix to examine accessible routes during a lift outage; a stair-only alternative is not usable by every passenger. Coverage is meaningful only relative to its defined denominator.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-33-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「電梯停用替代路徑」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Alternative routes during lift outages\" is correct?","options":["本單元以角色任務矩陣檢查電梯停用後的可達路徑，不能把需要樓梯的替代線視為所有旅客可用。","測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Use a user-task matrix to examine accessible routes during a lift outage; a stair-only alternative is not usable by every passenger.","One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本單元以角色任務矩陣檢查電梯停用後的可達路徑，不能把需要樓梯的替代線視為所有旅客可用。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Use a user-task matrix to examine accessible routes during a lift outage; a stair-only alternative is not usable by every passenger. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":1,"sequence":33},{"id":"b383-v16-34","title":"電梯停用替代路徑：定量估算","titleEn":"Alternative routes during lift outages: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-33"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「電梯停用替代路徑」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Alternative routes during lift outages” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-34-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。公式 y=tested/total，代入得 y=0.8 1。邊界：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Formula y=tested/total gives y=0.8 1. Boundary: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-34-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「電梯停用替代路徑」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Alternative routes during lift outages\", which statement holds?","options":["平面圖上最短的路徑一定是每位旅客最快的路徑","原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。","出口每秒通過人數穩定就能證明站內沒有排隊"],"optionsEn":["The shortest route on a plan is always the fastest route for every passenger.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases.","Stable exit throughput proves that no queue is forming inside the station."],"answer":1,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：已執行案例 tested=72 cases；已定義案例 total=90 cases。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: executed cases tested=72 cases; defined cases total=90 cases. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"model","order":2,"sequence":34},{"id":"b383-v16-35","title":"電梯停用替代路徑：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Alternative routes during lift outages: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-34"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「電梯停用替代路徑」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Alternative routes during lift outages” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「電梯停用替代路徑」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For alternative routes during lift outages, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「電梯停用替代路徑」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for alternative routes during lift outages, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-35-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。以「電梯停用替代路徑」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. For alternative routes during lift outages, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-35-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把已執行案例 tested 從 72 改成 73 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 0.8 變為 0.811111 1。先說明「電梯停用替代路徑」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only executed cases tested from 72 to 73 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 0.8 to 0.811111 1. Explain the causal direction for alternative routes during lift outages, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「電梯停用替代路徑」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Alternative routes during lift outages\"?","options":["只看一次讀值或外觀即可判定合格，不需要基準點、參考試體或重複量測。","整個大廳平均密度低就能保證每個出口都不擁擠","建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。"],"optionsEn":["A single reading or a visual impression is enough to accept the work; no datum, reference specimen or repeat measurement is needed.","A low concourse-average density guarantees that every exit is uncrowded.","Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立需求到案例的一對多追溯表，將未測、失敗與不適用分開，抽查原始證據。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Build requirement-to-case traceability, separate untested, failed and inapplicable cases, and sample raw evidence. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"verification","order":3,"sequence":35},{"id":"b383-v16-36","title":"電梯停用替代路徑：失效診斷","titleEn":"Alternative routes during lift outages: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-35"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「電梯停用替代路徑」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Alternative routes during lift outages” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「電梯停用替代路徑」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for alternative routes during lift outages. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：計數式已知案例覆蓋，不是失效機率或安全完整性量化。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Count-based coverage of known cases, not a probability of failure or a safety-integrity measure.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「測試覆蓋率達到百分之百就等於零故障風險」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"One hundred percent test coverage means zero failure risk.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-36-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。回到「電梯停用替代路徑」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Trace the input chain for alternative routes during lift outages. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-36-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「電梯停用替代路徑」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Alternative routes during lift outages\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。","裂縫或異常只出現一次就可以忽略，不需要記錄或追蹤。","所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果"],"optionsEn":["Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised.","A crack or anomaly that appears only once can be ignored without logging or follow-up.","All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results."],"answer":0,"explanation":"縮小分母可讓覆蓋率看似提高，重複案例也可能掩蓋邊界狀態根本未被執行。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Shrinking the denominator makes coverage look better; duplicate cases can hide boundary states that were never exercised. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":9,"unitFacet":"failure","order":4,"sequence":36},{"id":"b383-v16-37","title":"跨層動線驗證安排：機制與系統路徑","titleEn":"Planning multilevel route verification: mechanism and system paths","estimatedMinutes":20,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-36"],"objective":"說明「跨層動線驗證安排」如何影響轉乘車站垂直動線的受力、變形、水流或訊號表現，並畫出相關輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界。","objectiveEn":"Explain how “Planning multilevel route verification” governs forces, deformation, flow or signals in “Vertical circulation in interchange stations”, and map the relevant inputs, transfer paths and boundaries.","instruction":"本單元安排不同到達波與設備停用組合的重播，保留初始排隊與協助人員配置以便重現結果。測試工時包含案例執行與環境設定、資料復原及證據整理。平行化只有在資源和狀態真正獨立時有效；把多個會修改同一狀態的測試同時執行，可能造成結果不可重現，表面節省時間卻增加診斷成本。解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。 師傅任務：以自由體圖、流路圖或訊號圖畫出相關物理量如何經過「跨層動線驗證安排」傳到系統邊界，標出哪些量由設計決定、哪些由材料、施工或環境決定，再用三句話寫出機制摘要。","instructionEn":"Plan replay across arrival waves and equipment outages, retaining initial queues and assistance staffing so results can be reproduced. Test effort includes case execution, setup, state restoration and evidence handling. Parallelism helps only when resources and state are genuinely independent. Concurrent tests modifying one shared state can become irreproducible, apparently saving execution time while increasing diagnostic cost. Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded. Mentor task: draw a free-body, flow or signal diagram showing how relevant physical quantities pass through “Planning multilevel route verification” to the system boundary, mark which quantities are fixed by design and which by materials, construction or environment, then summarise the mechanism in three sentences.","observation":"量級提示：原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。","observationEn":"Order-of-magnitude cue: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min.","failure":"常見誤解：「所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果」這個說法忽略了上述機制；請在系統圖上指出它錯在哪一個環節。","failureEn":"Common misconception: \"All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.\" It ignores the mechanism above; mark on your system diagram where it breaks down.","check":"系統圖標明「跨層動線驗證安排」的輸入、傳遞路徑與邊界；三句摘要能解釋本步列出的誤解為何不成立。","checkEn":"The system diagram shows inputs, transfer paths and boundaries for “Planning multilevel route verification”; the three-sentence summary explains why the listed misconception fails.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-37-k1","title":"跨層動線驗證安排","titleEn":"Planning multilevel route verification","text":"本單元安排不同到達波與設備停用組合的重播，保留初始排隊與協助人員配置以便重現結果。測試工時包含案例執行與環境設定、資料復原及證據整理。","textEn":"Plan replay across arrival waves and equipment outages, retaining initial queues and assistance staffing so results can be reproduced. Test effort includes case execution, setup, state restoration and evidence handling.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-37-k2","title":"誤解辨析","titleEn":"Misconception check","text":"誤解：所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果 正確的工程判斷必須回到傳力機制與量級。","textEn":"Misconception: All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results. Sound engineering judgement goes back to the load path and magnitude.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"關於「跨層動線驗證安排」，下列哪一項敘述正確？","questionEn":"Which statement about \"Planning multilevel route verification\" is correct?","options":["所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果","本單元安排不同到達波與設備停用組合的重播，保留初始排隊與協助人員配置以便重現結果。","兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加"],"optionsEn":["All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.","Plan replay across arrival waves and equipment outages, retaining initial queues and assistance staffing so results can be reproduced.","Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"本單元安排不同到達波與設備停用組合的重播，保留初始排隊與協助人員配置以便重現結果。 其餘選項是常見誤解。","explanationEn":"Plan replay across arrival waves and equipment outages, retaining initial queues and assistance staffing so results can be reproduced. The other options are common misconceptions."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"mechanism","order":5,"sequence":37},{"id":"b383-v16-38","title":"跨層動線驗證安排：定量估算","titleEn":"Planning multilevel route verification: quantitative estimate","estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-37"],"objective":"以數值模型估算「跨層動線驗證安排」的關鍵量，並判斷幾何、速度、荷載或材料參數改變時結果的方向與幅度。","objectiveEn":"Estimate the key quantities of “Planning multilevel route verification” with a numerical model and judge the direction and size of change when geometry, speed, load or material parameters move.","instruction":"依下列模型逐步重算：原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。公式 y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60，代入得 y=19 h。邊界：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。 師傅任務：保留單位重算一次，再只改變一個輸入（連續量可增加 10%；計數須保持整數；分貝量使用加減值），預測並計算輸出的變化，說明它是線性、平方或更高次方的關係，並指出規範或設計上通常如何處理這個敏感度。","instructionEn":"Recalculate step by step: Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Formula y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60 gives y=19 h. Boundary: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded. Mentor task: redo the calculation keeping units, then change one input (for example +10% for a continuous quantity; retain integers for counts and use additive changes for decibels), predict and compute the output change, state whether the dependence is linear, quadratic or steeper, and note how codes or designers usually handle this sensitivity.","observation":"如何核對：逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。","observationEn":"How to cross-check: Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns.","failure":"計算陷阱：單位換算錯誤、把教學假設當成真實設計值、混淆標稱值與設計值（未乘載重或強度係數），或只看結果不檢查數量級，都會讓後續設計判斷失準。","failureEn":"Calculation traps: unit slips, treating teaching assumptions as real design values, mixing nominal and factored values, or accepting a result without checking its magnitude will mislead later design decisions.","check":"依模型顯示精度重現數值，列出單位與取整方式，並提交一個參數改變後的敏感度計算與工程解釋。","checkEn":"Reproduce the model values to their displayed precision, state units and rounding, and submit a sensitivity calculation for one changed parameter with an engineering explanation.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-38-k1","title":"定量模型","titleEn":"Quantitative model","text":"原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。公式 y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60，代入得 y=19 h。邊界：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。","textEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Formula y=(cases*minutes+setup)/60 gives y=19 h. Boundary: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-38-k2","title":"模型邊界","titleEn":"Model boundary","text":"本步數值為教學假設或公開資料的簡化；套用到實際工程前，必須依規範荷載組合、材料試驗與現場量測重新計算並由技師簽證。","textEn":"These numbers are teaching assumptions or simplified public data; before applying them to a real system, recalculate with code load combinations, material tests and site measurements, certified by a qualified engineer.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"依「跨層動線驗證安排」的定量模型，下列哪一項敘述成立？","questionEn":"According to the quantitative model for \"Planning multilevel route verification\", which statement holds?","options":["只要坡道平均坡度適當就不用檢查平台與橫坡","平均人數關係能直接預測任何瞬間的最大擁擠程度","原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。"],"optionsEn":["An acceptable mean ramp slope removes the need to check landings and cross-slope.","A mean occupancy relation directly predicts the maximum crowding at every instant.","Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min."],"answer":2,"explanation":"原創假想教學輸入：測試案例數 cases=120 cases；平均案例時間 minutes=8 min/case；設定與恢復時間 setup=180 min。 重算時請保留單位。","explanationEn":"Original hypothetical teaching inputs: test cases cases=120 cases; mean case duration minutes=8 min/case; setup and recovery time setup=180 min. Keep units when recalculating."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"model","order":6,"sequence":38},{"id":"b383-v16-39","title":"跨層動線驗證安排：試驗與驗證","titleEn":"Planning multilevel route verification: testing and verification","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-38"],"objective":"設計一項可重複的試驗、量測或檢查，驗證「跨層動線驗證安排」是否符合模型與規範預期，並在量測前訂出允收準則與停工點。","objectiveEn":"Design a repeatable test, measurement or inspection that verifies whether “Planning multilevel route verification” meets the model and code expectation, fixing acceptance criteria and hold points before measuring.","instruction":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。以「跨層動線驗證安排」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。 師傅任務：把上述方法寫成試驗或量測計畫，列出儀器與感測器、基準點或參考試體、步驟、比較對象、允收準則與停工點，並估計三項主要不確定度來源。","instructionEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. For planning multilevel route verification, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism. Mentor task: turn this into a test or measurement plan listing instruments and sensors, datums or reference specimens, procedure, comparison baseline, acceptance criteria and hold points, and estimate the three largest uncertainty contributions.","observation":"現場實務：只把測試案例數 cases 從 120 改成 121 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 19 變為 19.1333 h。先說明「跨層動線驗證安排」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","observationEn":"Site practice: Change only test cases cases from 120 to 121 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 19 to 19.1333 h. Explain the causal direction for planning multilevel route verification, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","failure":"注意干擾：省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。 只量一次、沒有可追溯的基準，或不記錄溫度、速度與操作條件，就無法分辨真正的偏差與量測誤差。","failureEn":"Watch for interference: Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. A single reading, no traceable datum, or unrecorded temperature, speed and operating conditions make real deviations indistinguishable from measurement error.","check":"提交試驗或量測計畫：儀器、基準、步驟、允收準則、停工點與不確定度預算，並說明如何判定合格或不合格、由誰簽認。","checkEn":"Submit the test or measurement plan: instruments, datums, procedure, acceptance criteria, hold points and uncertainty budget, with the pass/fail rule and who signs it off.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-39-k1","title":"驗證方法","titleEn":"Verification method","text":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。以「跨層動線驗證安排」為驗證目標，先寫出預期變化方向及可分辨的替代原因，再保存原始讀值、單位、校正版本與時間窗。只有比較同一系統邊界的資料，才判定殘差是否支持這項機制。","textEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. For planning multilevel route verification, state the expected direction and distinguishable alternative causes before collecting data. Retain raw readings, units, calibration version and observation window. Compare evidence within the same system boundary before deciding whether the residual supports this mechanism.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-39-k2","title":"現場實務","titleEn":"Site practice","text":"只把測試案例數 cases 從 120 改成 121 cases（增加一個可計數單位），其餘輸入固定。重算結果應由 19 變為 19.1333 h。先說明「跨層動線驗證安排」中變化的因果方向，再檢查適用邊界是否仍成立，提交計算與一個可反駁此解釋的觀測。","textEn":"Change only test cases cases from 120 to 121 cases (increase by one whole count), holding other inputs fixed. Recalculate 19 to 19.1333 h. Explain the causal direction for planning multilevel route verification, check that the stated boundary still holds, and submit the calculation plus one observation that could refute the explanation.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"要驗證「跨層動線驗證安排」，下列哪一個做法最恰當？","questionEn":"Which approach best verifies \"Planning multilevel route verification\"?","options":["逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。","不確定度太難估計，報告中只寫最佳值即可。","電梯每小時往返次數可以直接當作每小時服務人數"],"optionsEn":["Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns.","Uncertainty is too hard to estimate, so the report may state only the best value.","Elevator round trips per hour can directly be treated as passengers served per hour."],"answer":0,"explanation":"逐案記錄前置狀態、執行時間與復原時間，分開列出正常完成和失敗重測。 驗證需要基準、重複性與事先訂定的允收準則。","explanationEn":"Record preconditions, execution and restoration for every case, separating normal completion from failure reruns. Verification needs a datum, repeatability and acceptance criteria fixed in advance."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"verification","order":7,"sequence":39},{"id":"b383-v16-40","title":"跨層動線驗證安排：失效診斷","titleEn":"Planning multilevel route verification: failure diagnosis","estimatedMinutes":25,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"prerequisiteIds":["b383-v16-39"],"objective":"從症狀倒推「跨層動線驗證安排」的失效或劣化原因，提出能區分原因的檢查、矯正與預防措施。","objectiveEn":"Work back from symptoms to the failure or deterioration causes of “Planning multilevel route verification” and propose discriminating checks, corrective actions and prevention.","instruction":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。回到「跨層動線驗證安排」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。 師傅任務：建立失效樹——症狀、兩個以上可能原因、能區分它們的量測或檢測，以及矯正與預防措施；並說明此失效如何影響整體系統的安全、使用性、耐久或營運。","instructionEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Trace the input chain for planning multilevel route verification. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion. Mentor task: build a fault tree with the symptom, at least two candidate causes, a measurement or inspection that tells them apart, and corrective and preventive actions; explain how the failure affects whole-system safety, serviceability, durability or operation.","observation":"連結機制：解釋前先固定模型適用範圍：確定平均案例時間的串行估算，未含故障重測與資源衝突。","observationEn":"Link to the mechanism: Before interpreting the result, fix its domain: Serial estimate with deterministic mean case time; failure reruns and resource conflicts are excluded.","failure":"誤判風險：若相信「所有整合測試都可以同時執行而完全不影響結果」，上述症狀可能被錯誤處理而反覆出現。","failureEn":"Misdiagnosis risk: believing \"All integration tests can run simultaneously without affecting results.\" leads to mishandling the symptom so it keeps returning.","check":"完成失效樹與矯正措施，指出哪一項量測或檢測能最快確認根因、需要哪些人簽認，以及如何防止再發。","checkEn":"Complete the fault tree and corrective actions, name the measurement or inspection that confirms the root cause fastest, who must sign off, and how recurrence is prevented.","knowledge":[{"id":"b383-v16-40-k1","title":"失效模式","titleEn":"Failure mode","text":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。回到「跨層動線驗證安排」的輸入鏈逐項定位；先重播單一異常，再比較共同原因的組合。保留不確定項，避免為了讓結果符合預期而刪去不利證據。","textEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Trace the input chain for planning multilevel route verification. Replay one anomaly first, then compare common-cause combinations. Retain uncertain observations rather than discarding adverse evidence to force the expected conclusion.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]},{"id":"b383-v16-40-k2","title":"根因確認","titleEn":"Root-cause confirmation","text":"根因必須以可區分的量測或檢測確認；只補強外觀、更換構件或放寬允收值可能掩蓋問題。","textEn":"Confirm the root cause with a discriminating measurement or inspection; cosmetic repair, swapping components or relaxing limits can mask the problem.","sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"]}],"quiz":{"question":"在「跨層動線驗證安排」出現異常時，下列哪一項判斷最合理？","questionEn":"When \"Planning multilevel route verification\" shows distress, which diagnosis is most reasonable?","options":["先更換最貴的構件；只要症狀消失，就代表已找到根因。","省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。","兩條走道接到同一狹窄出口時容量仍可直接相加"],"optionsEn":["Replace the most expensive component first; if the symptom disappears, the root cause has been found.","Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort.","Two corridors feeding one narrow exit always have directly additive capacity."],"answer":1,"explanation":"省略復原步驟會讓前案狀態污染後案，僅報告成功案例時間則低估總測試成本。 需以量測區分可能原因。","explanationEn":"Omitted restoration contaminates later tests with earlier state; reporting only successful durations understates total effort. Discriminate candidate causes by measurement."},"unit":10,"unitFacet":"failure","order":8,"sequence":40}],"order":5}],"sourceIds":["v16s-fta-emergency","v16s-passenger-flow","v16s-rb-station","v16s-taipei-main-reference","v16s-kings-cross-reference"],"curriculumVersion":16,"stepCount":40,"estimatedMinutes":1000,"flowDiagram":"assets/diagrams/v16-b383-zh.svg","flowDiagramEn":"assets/diagrams/v16-b383-en.svg"}};
